{
  "dom_id": "step-q110268",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "The point $P$ with coordinates $(1,2)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x).$ Which of the following points must lie on $y=f(x+5)+2?$",
  "worked_solution": "The graph of $y=f(x+5)+2$  is a translation of the graph of $y=f(x)$ by $5$ units to the *left* and $2$ units up. So the $y$-coordinate increases by $2$ and the $x$-coordinate decreases by $5.$\n\nWe know that the point $(1,2)$ lies on $y=f(x).$ Therefore, the point $(1-5,2+2)=(-4,4)$ must lie on $y=f(x+5)+2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14214993/assets/00557550846a020f437c6187dfe237b4e1cb874eca2bb1cf2bd70416e0e8d97c.png)",
